 "notes": "Controller: state machine per cube (target then second). Hover above cube (joint-space move for 2nd cube via offline IK seed, then Cartesian damped-least-squares IK keeping palm down; hand yaw chosen among cube-face-aligned candidates by offline kinematic feasibility), descend, close hand (closure ramp to 1), lift, transit to bin with closed-loop on cube position (in-hand offset), release from ~2.7 cm above the rim at opposite bin corners (first cube +x/-y corner, second at opposite corner computed from measured first cube) so both cubes fit, retreat, finally return to home pose. Anti-windup clamp relative to measured joints. Known weaknesses (~50% success on practice seeds): second cube sometimes lands tilted on/against first cube in the left bin (hand finger geometry limits reach near bin walls; cube drift on release); cubes near the torso (x<0.18, y\u2248-0.11) sometimes cause the second pick to stall; occasional first-grasp failure with some yaws (cube dropped on table).",
